BT 1 0 0 1 0 44.5 Tm 13.5 TL /F2 9.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Observation.) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf ( 549 passengers \(61.6%\) died and 342 \(38.4%\) survived, an imbalance ratio of about ) Tj /F2 9.5 Tf (1.6 : 1) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf (. This is a) Tj T* -0.087773 Tw /F2 9.5 Tf (mild imbalance) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf (: not balanced perfectly, but not severe \(like 95/5 fraud data\). Accuracy alone would still look decent \(a) Tj T* 0 Tw (model that always predicts "died" gets 61.6%\), so in modelling we should also report precision, recall, F1 and) Tj T* (ROC-AUC, and use stratified train/test splits. Class weights can be tried but heavy resampling is not needed.) Tj T* ET
