BT 1 0 0 1 0 58 Tm 13.5 TL /F2 9.5 Tf 0 0 0 rg (Interpretation.) Tj /F1 9.5 Tf ( Female passengers \(pink\) are mostly marked as survivors across the age-fare plane, whereas blue) Tj T* (male points are mostly non-survivors except at young ages or very high fares. The point plot makes the class-sex) Tj T* (interaction clear: the gap between women and men is huge in First and Second class, and shrinks in Third class) Tj T* (because third-class women fared much worse. Confidence intervals are widest for First-class men and women) Tj T* (because of smaller group sizes.) Tj T* ET
